From 6f81debeec923b39a512b022238344b4ee2d23df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:26:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 110/117] hydra: UsdPreviewSurface switches, texture colour
 spaces and wrap modes

UsdPreviewSurface picks one of four mappings by useSpecularWorkflow and
opacityThreshold: in the specular workflow the principled's IOR comes from
specularColor's largest component and the colour tints the specular; in
the metallic workflow specularColor is ignored, as USD says. A threshold
above zero cuts out below it (K-65).

Texture colour spaces (K-66): UsdImaging moves sourceColorSpace and a
MaterialX file input's colorSpace metadata into the parameter's colour-space
field, which is now read. Names resolve against the active OCIO config
(ColorSpaceManager::resolve_texture_colorspace), so sRGB reaches Houdini's
config as its sRGB texture space instead of a builtin it does not know.
Translated image nodes start in auto instead of the constructor's
scene_linear, and auto picks the config's sRGB texture space for a file
tagged sRGB. wrapS/wrapT translate to Cycles' extension names (repeat ->
periodic, useMetadata -> black).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
